  ('production', 'Christopher Lee Schulze', 'Has anyone done a TR for a statutory employee? Client I''m working on has W-2 income and taxprolink requires me to put schedule C with matching info from W-2, but whenever I do this it doubles his taxable income. Just curious if anyone has seen anything like this before?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:30:34+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Willow S', '@Lucille is our new Tax Pre and may know the answer', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:31:40+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Lucille', 'Have you checked  box 13 for statutory employee', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:33:45+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Christopher Lee Schulze', 'Yes and I also checked it when I do the Schedule C, and it still doubles the income', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:34:07+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Lucille', 'Also when entering the expenses in Schedule C do not  reenter the gross income', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:34:22+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Lucille', 'Also make sure the W2 is linked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:34:56+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Lucille', 'leave the sales /income line on Sch C blank', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:35:16+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Christopher Lee Schulze', 'How can I link them? When I researched it said the same thing, but not sure how', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:35:30+00:00'),
  ('production', 'Lucille', 'Wait a second', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-21T13:36:08+00:00'),
