I am requesting an abatement of penalties assessed for tax year 2014 on behalf of my client, *Michael [Last Name]*, due to reasonable cause.
Michael is an over-the-road truck driver who spends extended periods away from home, often for weeks at a time. His occupation has made it extremely difficult to maintain consistent financial records and communication with tax professionals. As a result, he developed poor bookkeeping practices that led to the delay in resolving his 2014 tax liabilities.
Additionally, Michael is currently in the process of liquidating his investment property to resolve outstanding tax liabilities and improve compliance moving forward.
Michael did not willfully neglect his responsibilities and is taking corrective steps. Given the circumstances and his willingness to make good on his obligations, we respectfully request that the IRS grant reasonable cause abatement under § 6651(a)(3) and any associated penalties under codes 166, 170, and 276.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-08T14:28:21+00:00'),
  ('nashville-tax-soltuions-paras', 'U096WS8LT3Q', 'this is a great start, but we want to add a bit of fluff for lack of better term. If you look at this account transcripts, you can see how much money he made in certain years, and put yourself in his shoes. Would you be able to pay your bills with the amount of money he was making? Make sure your bills were paid, your rent, food etc? Now if he had paid his taxes, how would that have changed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-08T14:30:12+00:00'),
  ('nashville-tax-soltuions-paras', 'alexandra', 'is this fluffy enough?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-08T16:57:48+00:00'),
  ('nashville-tax-soltuions-paras', 'alexandra', 'To Whom It May Concern:
I am submitting this request on behalf of my client under *IRC §6651(a)(3)* to seek *abatement of a $1,494.91 penalty* assessed for *failure to pay the tax due following a notice and demand for payment* for the 2014 tax year.
My client, an over-the-road truck driver operating as a sole proprietor, experienced serious financial and administrative hardship during the year in question and the period following. He was unaware of the balance due until formal IRS correspondence was received, and at that point lacked both the liquidity and professional guidance to resolve the issue within the required time frame.
Since that time, my client has made a good-faith effort to resolve the situation. He has retained tax representation, organized financial records, and is in the process of preparing an investment property for sale in order to resolve the outstanding tax debt. These steps reflect a clear intent to comply and take responsibility.
In accordance with *IRM 20.1.2.2.3* and IRS guidance, we believe these facts support a finding of *reasonable cause* for penalty relief under *§6651(a)(3)*. My client did not willfully neglect his obligations, and the failure to pay promptly was due to factors beyond his control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-08T16:57:52+00:00'),
  ('nashville-tax-soltuions-paras', 'alexandra', 'So I did a compliance check and the rep said for 2016 there is a shared responsibility for 1125.28 the balanced owed is 19,127.87  which do I use?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-08T18:17:11+00:00'),
